rew atmosphere, but has communication difficulty and egocentric, and not willing to further education (adaptability). B is strong on reliability and stress, but cooperation issues. D strong on problem solving and responsibility, but arrogance and weak leadership. A strong technical, leadership, but unorganized and poor at criticism.\n\nWhich candidate best balances? Probably Candidate C, because reliability, decision quality, positive crew atmosphere outweigh communication difficulty? But communication is important for safety. However, egocentric and communication difficulty could be serious. B's uncooperative is also serious. D's arrogance also serious. A's unorganized could affect reliability.\n\nThus C might be best overall, but we need to discuss. I will propose Candidate C as current recommendation, citing reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere, but note concerns about communication and education willingness.\n\nWe need to reference existing discussion: none yet, but we can say \"I would like to start by focusing on Candidate C\". That's okay.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nProceed."}
